   flex item in its slide row (see Slide.tsx). Two independent, composable axes:
   - Space-sharing: .grow / .grow-2 / .grow-3 / .no-grow (flex-grow weight)
   - Width ceiling: .narrow / .wide / .full-width (max-width, layered on top of grow)
   - Alignment: .left-align / .right-align / .center-align (margin, only visible
     when there's free space left in the row - i.e. the panel isn't also .grow)
   All rules use !important since they're meant to override the row's own default
   per-panel sizing (see getPanelSx in story-styles.ts), not just add to it. */

/* --- Space-sharing between multiple panels in one row --- */
.grow {
  flex: 1 1 0% !important;
}

.grow-2 {
  flex: 2 1 0% !important;
}

.grow-3 {
  flex: 3 1 0% !important;
}

.no-grow {
  flex: 0 0 auto !important;
}

/* --- Alignment (push within whatever free space the row has left) --- */
.left-align {
  margin-right: auto !important;
  margin-left: 0 !important;
}

.right-align {
  margin-left: auto !important;
  margin-right: 0 !important;
}

.center-align {
  margin-left: auto !important;
  margin-right: auto !important;
}

/* --- Width ceilings - min(Xpx, 100%) shrinks to fit narrow viewports instead
   of overflowing; combine with a grow/alignment class above as needed --- */
.narrow {
  max-width: min(600px, 100%) !important;
}

.wide {
  max-width: min(1200px, 100%) !important;
}

.full-width {
  max-width: 100% !important;
}
